SELENE (KAGUYA) lunar limb profile — kaguya_lalt.bin
  Source data: SELENE Global Grid Topographic Data of the Moon (LALT_GGT_NUM),
  dataset sln-l-lalt-5-topo-ggt-num-v2.0, version 2.0, published 2017.
  Origin of the data: ISAS/JAXA.
  Provided by the SELENE (KAGUYA) Data Archive (DARTS), ISAS/JAXA:
    https://darts.isas.jaxa.jp/datasets/darts:sln-l-lalt-5-topo-ggt-num-v2.0

  Acknowledgement, as requested by the SELENE Data Archive:
    "We thank the SELENE(KAGUYA) LALT team and the SELENE Data Archive for
     providing the SELENE(KAGUYA) data. SELENE is a Japanese mission developed
     and operated by JAXA."

  Modifications: the original PDS3 fixed-width table (1/16 degree global grid,
  2880 x 5760 samples) was converted to a float32 elevation grid and resampled
  into a limb-radius profile table on a 1 degree grid of selenographic
  (libration) longitude and latitude and a 0.1 degree grid of position angle,
  taking max (R + h) cos(alpha) over a +/-9 degree arc per direction; the
  result is stored in this project's own zlib-compressed LLB1 container.

